    },
    sections: [
      {
        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Stealing Bundles',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Stealing Bundles (also known as Stealing the Old Man's Bundle) is a simple fishing card game for two or more players, popular with children. It is similar to Casino but simplified. Players capture face-up cards from the table by matching their rank. Captured cards are stacked in a 'bundle'. The unique twist is that players can steal an opponent's entire bundle by matching the top card.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "A children's fishing game also known as Steal the Old Man's Bundle or Steal Pile. A very similar game is played in Argentina as Casita Robada and in Italy as Rubamazzo. It is classified as a fishing game and shares capture-by-rank and bundle-building with games like Casino but is simplified for young players.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '2, 3 or 4 players. First dealer is chosen by everyone drawing a card; highest card deals (tied players draw again).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard 52-card pack; suits are ignored for matching (only rank matters).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard 52-card pack; suits are ignored for matching (only rank matters).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Dealer gives each player 5 cards; remaining cards are dealt face-up to the table. Play starts to the left of the dealer.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Variations',
            subtitle: 'Known ways this game changes',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'list',
                style: 'unordered',
                items: [
                  {
                    text: 'Standard: Five cards each; remainder to table; capture by rank, steal bundle by matching top, or trail.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Hand size variant: Some house rules use a different number of cards per player (e.g. 4 or 6).',
                  },
                ],
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
